From cb11e9ab7bddffaf0e55e62cc49969509f7c3253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:34:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] feat(api): list the tenant's audit records

GET /api/v1/audit-events returns the audit records of the caller's
tenant, newest first, and needs the read scope. It accepts limit (1 to
1000, default 100, like the list endpoints), pageToken and an optional
correlationId filter, and returns {items, count, nextPageToken}; the
token is only present when there is another page. Like the other
routes it answers 503 REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE while the registry is not
ready and echoes X-Correlation-Id in its error responses.

AuditLog.list_page pages by position (timestamp, then audit id), so
records written while a client pages do not repeat or skip records on
later pages. A new index on (tenant_id, correlation_id, timestamp)
serves the filter.

The page token is signed like the resource list tokens and with the
same key. Their signing code moves from the registry into
forgemesh.controlplane.pagetokens without changing the token format
(the module now also creates the registry_meta table, and its single
InvalidPageTokenError is still exported by the registry package). The
audit log loads the page_token_key row of its database, which in the
control plane is the registry's database. The signed scope names the
list, the tenant and the correlationId filter: a token issued for
another tenant or filter, a resource list token, a modified token or
one from another database is rejected with 400, and tokens stay valid
across restarts. The token is not a credential: the query is always
limited to the caller's tenant.

The operation and the AuditEvent / AuditEventList schemas are in the
OpenAPI document, and the contract drift test covers the operation.
The Go gateway does not forward this path yet, so it is only reachable
on the control plane itself.
